                <pb facs="0187" n="177" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg177"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/2524: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-25T18:00:00+03:00">April 25, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 26—3:12 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1432. In reply to my inquiry as to any developments in the Soviet-Rumanian
                    situation Molotov informed me that Maniu’s proposal made by Prince Stirbey to
                    break away from Antonescu and to form a new government in Soviet-occupied
                    Rumania, although acceptable to the Soviet Government, was not considered as
                    having been made seriously. He said that there were yet no different [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">definite?</hi>] indications that Maniu would follow such
                    a course.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
